                </section>

                <section class="faq-section content-section">
                    <h2 class="section-title">Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>
                    <div class="faq-index card">
                        <h3>FAQ Index</h3>
                        <ul>
                            <li><a href="#faq-item-1">What is a standard tip percentage for a restaurant?</a></li>
                            <li><a href="#faq-item-2">Should I tip on the pre-tax or post-tax amount of the bill?</a></li>
                            <li><a href="#faq-item-3">How much should I tip for delivery services?</a></li>
                            <li><a href="#faq-item-4">Is it okay not to tip if the service was bad?</a></li>
                            <li><a href="#faq-item-5">How does this tip calculator handle splitting the bill?</a></li>
                            <li><a href="#faq-item-6">Can I enter a custom tip percentage?</a></li>
                            <li><a href="#faq-item-7">Do I need to tip for takeout orders?</a></li>
                            <li><a href="#faq-item-8">What about tipping in other countries?</a></li>
                            <li><a href="#faq-item-9">How much should I tip for services like a haircut or taxi?</a></li>
                            <li><a href="#faq-item-10">What if the restaurant automatically adds a gratuity or service charge?</a></li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-item" id="faq-item-1"> <h3> <button class="accordion" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-panel-1"> What is a standard tip percentage for a restaurant? <span class="accordion-icon"></span> </button> </h3> <div class="panel" id="faq-panel-1" role="region"> <p>In the United States, a standard tip for good service at a restaurant is typically between 15% and 20% of the pre-tax bill. Some people choose to tip more for excellent service.</p> </div> </div>
                    <div class="faq-item" id="faq-item-2"> <h3> <button class="accordion" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-panel-2"> Should I tip on the pre-tax or post-tax amount of the bill? <span class="accordion-icon"></span> </button> </h3> <div class="panel" id="faq-panel-2" role="region"> <p>It is customary to calculate the tip based on the pre-tax amount of the bill. However, some people prefer to tip on the total amount for simplicity.</p> </div> </div>
                    <div class="faq-item" id="faq-item-3"> <h3> <button class="accordion" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-panel-3"> How much should I tip for delivery services? <span class="accordion-icon"></span> </button> </h3> <div class="panel" id="faq-panel-3" role="region"> <p>For food delivery, a tip of 15-20% is common, similar to restaurant dining. For grocery delivery, 10-15% or a flat amount might be appropriate depending on the size and difficulty of the order.</p> </div> </div>
                    <div class="faq-item" id="faq-item-4"> <h3> <button class="accordion" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-panel-4"> Is it okay not to tip if the service was bad? <span class="accordion-icon"></span> </button> </h3> <div class="panel" id="faq-panel-4" role="region"> <p>Tipping is generally a reflection of service quality. If service was exceptionally poor, some people choose to tip a lower percentage or speak to management. However, in many service industries, workers rely on tips for a significant portion of their income.</p> </div> </div>
                    <div class="faq-item" id="faq-item-5"> <h3> <button class="accordion" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-panel-5"> How does this tip calculator handle splitting the bill? <span class="accordion-icon"></span> </button> </h3> <div class="panel" id="faq-panel-5" role="region"> <p>Our calculator divides the total bill (including the calculated tip) evenly by the number of people you specify. It ensures everyone pays an equal share of both the main bill and the gratuity.</p> </div> </div>
                    <div class="faq-item" id="faq-item-6"> <h3> <button class="accordion" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-panel-6"> Can I enter a custom tip percentage? <span class="accordion-icon"></span> </button> </h3> <div class="panel" id="faq-panel-6" role="region"> <p>Yes! While we provide quick buttons for common percentages like 15%, 18%, and 20%, there is also a field where you can enter any custom tip percentage you prefer.</p> </div> </div>
                    <div class="faq-item" id="faq-item-7"> <h3> <button class="accordion" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-panel-7"> Do I need to tip for takeout orders? <span class="accordion-icon"></span> </button> </h3> <div class="panel" id="faq-panel-7" role="region"> <p>Tipping for takeout is not always expected to the same degree as dine-in service, but it is often appreciated, especially if the order is large or complex. A smaller tip of 10-15% or a few dollars is a common gesture.</p> </div> </div>
                    <div class="faq-item" id="faq-item-8"> <h3> <button class="accordion" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-panel-8"> What about tipping in other countries? <span class="accordion-icon"></span> </button> </h3> <div class="panel" id="faq-panel-8" role="region"> <p>Tipping customs vary significantly around the world. In some countries, tipping is not customary or is even included in a service charge. It’s always a good idea to research local tipping etiquette when traveling.</p> </div> </div>
                    <div class="faq-item" id="faq-item-9"> <h3> <button class="accordion" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-panel-9"> How much should I tip for services like a haircut or taxi? <span class="accordion-icon"></span> </button> </h3> <div class="panel" id="faq-panel-9" role="region"> <p>For hairdressers, stylists, and barbers, a 15-20% tip is standard. For taxi or rideshare drivers, 10-20% of the fare is common.</p> </div> </div>
                    <div class="faq-item" id="faq-item-10"> <h3> <button class="accordion" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-panel-10"> What if the restaurant automatically adds a gratuity or service charge? <span class="accordion-icon"></span> </button> </h3> <div class="panel" id="faq-panel-10" role="region"> <p>Always check your bill for an automatic gratuity, especially for large parties. If a service charge is already included, you generally do not need to add an additional tip unless you feel the service was exceptional and warrants it.</p> </div> </div>
                </section>
             </article>
